# Design: Layered post-v0.3.2 hardening

## Problem
The v0.3.2 black-box assessment passed but identified residual operational risks: unsandboxed children, inherited non-provider credentials, minimal-container installer assumptions, and incomplete release/provider evidence.

## Approach
Keep compatibility-preserving defaults while adding explicit controls: a common-secret deny preset, value-safe environment diagnostics, fail-closed Bubblewrap containment, portable temporary-directory selection, SBOM attestations, and credential-backed provider smoke infrastructure.

## Key Trade-offs
- Secret filtering and containment remain opt-in so existing cloud and filesystem workflows do not silently break.
- Bubblewrap restricts network and writes but deliberately does not claim to hide readable host files.
- Live provider tests are manually dispatched because they require repository credentials and incur external calls.

## Verification
421 Rust tests, strict Clippy, documentation/workflow checks, installer and provider self-tests, telemetry tests, release build, and crate packaging passed before release.
